[E0303] Error: cannot apply `*` to `f64` and `f32`
    ╭─[ err/589_a_literal_local_keeps_its_own/main.wip:12:21 ]
    │
 11 │     loudest = loudest.max(1.0)
    │               ───┬───
    │                  ╰───── its first use, which says nothing of its type
 12 │     val a = loudest * halfX
    │             ───┬─── ┬ ──┬──
    │                ╰───────────── `f64`
    │                     │   │
    │                     ╰──────── operands of different types
    │                         │
    │                         ╰──── `f32`
    │
    │ Help: write it where `loudest` is declared: `var loudest: f32 = …`
    │
    │ Note 1: a float is made another by `as`, which may round
    │
    │ Note 2: `loudest` is `f64`, its literal's own: a variable of a number literal takes its type from its first use, where that says one
────╯
