[E0301] Error: mismatched types
    ╭─[ err/589_a_literal_local_keeps_its_own/main.wip:18:21 ]
    │
 17 │     val later = () => count + 1
    │                       ──┬──
    │                         ╰──── its first use, which says nothing of its type
 18 │     val small: u8 = count
    │                ─┬   ──┬──
    │                 ╰────────── expected because of this type
    │                       │
    │                       ╰──── expected `u8`, found `i64`
    │
    │ Help: write it where `count` is declared: `val count: u8 = …`
    │
    │ Note 1: `count` is `i64`, its literal's own: a variable of a number literal takes its type from its first use, where that says one
    │
    │ Note 2: `u8` does not hold every value of `i64`, so it is not widened to it; `as` converts it, keeping the low bits of a value that does not fit
